From: XProtocol Bot
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Serve same-process completion-port traffic in-process.

Job systems post and dequeue completion packets on ports only their own threads use; every
NtSetIoCompletion and NtRemoveIoCompletion is a wineserver round trip (~3 us, ~90% of it kernel
time). Where Winds Meet does ~12.9 million of them per session on such ports. Keep the queue of
an unnamed, non-inheritable port in the process until it is used in a way only the server can
serve (file/socket bind, job association, duplication out of this process, handle-flag change,
NtSetIoCompletionEx, alertable dequeue, direct wait); then hand its packets to the server object
in order and let the server serve it from then on. WINE_INPROC_IOCP=0 disables it; +iocp traces
every port taken in-process and every demotion with its reason.
---
--- a/dlls/ntdll/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/Makefile.in
@@ -50,6 +50,7 @@
 	unix/debug.c \
 	unix/env.c \
 	unix/file.c \
+	unix/iocp.c \
 	unix/fsync.c \
 	unix/loader.c \
 	unix/loadorder.c \
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
@@ -5559,6 +5559,7 @@
         {
             FILE_COMPLETION_INFORMATION *info = ptr;
 
+            inproc_iocp_demote( info->CompletionPort, "file or socket bound" );
             SERVER_START_REQ( set_completion_info )
             {
                 req->handle   = wine_server_obj_handle( handle );
@@ -8409,6 +8410,7 @@
 
         if (len < sizeof(*p)) return STATUS_INVALID_BUFFER_SIZE;
 
+        inproc_iocp_demote( handle, "handle flags changed" );
         SERVER_START_REQ( set_handle_info )
         {
             req->handle = wine_server_obj_handle( handle );
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/iocp.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/iocp.c
@@ -0,0 +1,639 @@
